{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/838325-looking-for-online-changeling-2e-game","id":838325,"title":"Looking for online Changeling 2E game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T18:16:17-08:00","id":838325,"title":"Looking for online Changeling 2E game","content":"Pretty much as the title describes, I'd like to try playing a game of Changeling: The Lost, second edition, using the playtestable chunks that have been given out. The problem is that I'm not terribly familiar with the intricacies of Chronicles of Darkness, and in regards to Changeling I'm also not completely up to date on it. Certain rules I have a grasp of, others not so much, but what I've read has really gotten me motivated in making characters and I'd like to put them to use.<br /> <br /> If there's a group who wants to take me on, I'd be grateful and commit to absorbing the rules there are. I've primarily played online games, and usually use skype and google docs, though I'm open to other programs. Thanks for reading, and apologies if this is in the wrong section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 02-27-2016, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:03:10-08:00","id":843655,"title":"","content":"I don't have a group or anything, but I could run a 1-on-1 game for you, or for a few others if we can find any. Changeling is my second favorite gameline in CoD so I'd be happy to run with the playtestable chunks. What times would you be willing to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T18:26:08-08:00","id":844255,"title":"","content":"That's very kind of you to offer, and I'd be happy to accept. :-) In general my evenings/late afternoons are free, typically from Monday to Thursday at around 5pm, though my work schedule tends to go into flux and change days and hours (incidently, I'm Pacific Standard Time). Home Depot isn't usually static. What time zone are you in, since that can cause a dramatic shift in what times we play at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T03:48:45-08:00","id":844995,"title":"","content":"I live in New Zealand, and since the seasons are reversed in the southern hemisphere, that means the time difference changes whenever daylight savings rolls around. Complicating things even further is the fact that New Zealand and the USA take off/put on daylight savings time on different days. Good news is I'm used to this as a lot of my family lives in California, so I can update you on the time changes.<br /> <br /> Currently, I'm 19 hours ahead of you, or to put it another way, a day ahead but 5 hours behind. This will change to 4 hours behind on April 2nd (your time) when I'm putting all my clocks an hour back, and it'll change to 3 hours when you spring forward (not sure when that will be exactly, but I think it's at the end of April). My schedule's pretty free, but I would prefer Thursday evenings your time (that's Friday afternoons for me).<br /> <br /> Although there's another issue for this, and that's an idea for a chronicle, I don't really have one. I am very familiar with Changeling material, so I know how to capture the feeling and everything, I just don't have a plot idea to work with. Perhaps we could discuss it on Skype. I'll PM you my username.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 03-10-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:17:06-08:00","id":845233,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I hadn't expected such a time difference, but given what you've told me we can definitely make it work. I've talked with a couple of friends in or close to your time zone, and I have thought of the time difference as the way you put it (one day ahead and several hours behind). Thursday nights sound great to me, though I'll let you know if/when my schedule doesn't allow it. I do appreciate the time change elaborations too, since I was unaware of that level of change between your time and mine.<br /> <br /> Plot ideas are always a nuisance when you are deliberately pondering them. I compare inspiration/ideas to cats - they come when they darn well please, often when you don't want them to, and they'll be moody if you make them come to you. As for what I can provide, I was thinking of using an Elemental Changeling that I'd been making for a while, Cardiac Mask. Simply put, he's an amnesiac Changeling who was a &quot;Hero&quot; in his Keeper's realm, where &quot;Monsters&quot;, &quot;Civilians&quot; and &quot;Heroes&quot; were put into conflicts where one side had to survive above the others...and since that was the only way to get food or water in that realm, and nobody (aside from Heroes) who died stayed dead, it quickly developed into a stockholm syndrome-esc situation. Cardiac only got out because, as a Hero, he simply didn't get beaten into the routine of death and rebirth and realized how insane the situation was. Suffice to say, Cardiac's not exactly keen on being called a hero these days (in fact, being called one is a breaking point). I have a few other Changeling ideas, but none quite as developed as that (Cardiac's story is more developed, that's just the quick notes version).<br /> <br /> Message/request sent, and no offence taken for the keyword; I've gotten random requests over Skype myself, almost always bots. Here's hoping we can get a bit more of a group going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}